    "lawCode": "Add §1204-a, amd §517, R & SS L; amd §§612, 671 & 1340, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5837\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the retirement and social security law\nand the tax law, in relation to the\ntreatment of member contributions in accordance with the provisions of\nthe Internal Revenue Code\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThe purpose of this bill is to align\nthe contributions made by members of the New York State and Local\npolice and Fire retirement system pursuant to Tier V with the Federal\ninternal revenue code.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSections one of this bill would treat\nmember contributions as part of a member's salary for tax purposes.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nSimilar provisions exist with regard to all other NYS\nretirement systems which require contributions,\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nSee fiscal note.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
